item 5 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/5/measure".

item 5 measure is an assessment statement.

item 5 measure has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 5 measure has the judgement "Regulation (EU) 2022/2399".

item 5 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeAlignmentMeasure".

item 5 measure concerns the service interop 2.

item 5 measure has the description "Alignment with existing digital and sectorial policiesPlease list the applicable digital and sectorial policies identified".


item 6 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/6/measure".

item 6 measure is an assessment statement.

item 6 measure has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 6 measure has the judgement "The solution will alter the way actors interact with one another; paper documents will be replaced by electronic documents or messages, happening at a faster pace.
The solution will have a significant impact on the following stakeholders:
Economic operators involved inexternal trade in drug precursors, who apply for licences electronically via the new system.
EU Member Statescompetent authoritieswhoreceive applications for and issue licences
EUcountries’customsofficeswhocontrolcustoms declarationsofdrug precursorsandverifythe relevantlicences electronically.
The European Commission, which is responsible for the development and maintenance of the system, ensuring its functionality and compliance. The EU countries are responsible for connecting their national customs systems to the EU CSW-CERTEX, which in turn ensures connection to the central solution.".

item 6 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeOrganisationMeasure".

item 6 measure concerns the service interop 2.

item 6 measure has the description "Organisational measures for a smooth cross-border digital public services deliveryPlease list the governance measures foreseen".


item 7 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/7/measure".

item 7 measure is an assessment statement.

item 7 measure has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 7 measure has the judgement "Data management will prioritise usability, reliability, and security, and support agile updates to meet evolving legal and operational requirements.
The system will be aligned with the EU Customs Data Model (EUCDM) to ensure full interoperability with customs IT systems and compliance with EU customs legislation. Data elements required for import and export procedures will be harmonised and incorporated into future amendments to implementing and delegated regulations related to external trade in drug precursors.".

item 7 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeSharedMeasure".

item 7 measure concerns the service interop 2.

item 7 measure has the description "Measures taken to ensure a shared understanding of the dataPlease list such measures".


item 8 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/8/measure".

item 8 measure is an assessment statement.

item 8 measure has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 8 measure has the judgement "Interoperability with customs systems such as EU CSW-CERTEX and TARIC is foreseen.".

item 8 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeStandardsMeasure".

item 8 measure concerns the service interop 2.

item 8 measure has the description "Use of commonly agreed open technical specifications and standardsPlease list such measures".


